WEBVTT

00:34.193 --> 00:35.461
(This drama is a work of fiction.)

00:35.461 --> 00:36.696
(All characters, organizations,
and events in this drama are fictitious.)

00:36.696 --> 00:37.930
(This drama complied
with production guidelines...)

00:37.930 --> 00:39.165
(for filming child actors and animals.)

00:43.396 --> 00:44.497
Darn it.

00:46.418 --> 00:47.853
Where did those two run off to this time?

01:06.258 --> 01:07.392
Are you kidding me?

01:08.928 --> 01:10.363
Seo Anna...

01:23.943 --> 01:30.916
(Episode 3 Timing)

01:32.918 --> 01:35.721
(Parang-ri diver Jo Mi Hyun)

01:44.464 --> 01:46.733
This will help prevent fogging underwater.

01:49.002 --> 01:50.837
So you're coating them?

01:51.571 --> 01:54.074
The sea has its own clock.

01:55.675 --> 01:57.277
High tide, low tide, and the tidal cycle.

01:58.044 --> 01:59.145
I know that much.

01:59.446 --> 02:00.814
You knew that,

02:00.814 --> 02:02.549
but you went diving
when it was the most dangerous?

02:04.885 --> 02:05.819
Did I?

02:07.554 --> 02:08.822
You got swept away...

02:09.523 --> 02:10.991
because the current was too strong.

02:19.866 --> 02:21.868
The time when the current is weakest,

02:21.868 --> 02:24.337
between low tide and high tide,
is called slack tide.

02:25.205 --> 02:26.540
It's the only time...

02:26.907 --> 02:29.242
the sea allows divers into the water,
twice a day.

02:30.577 --> 02:32.612
And when's that?

02:34.447 --> 02:35.415
Right now.

02:40.954 --> 02:41.922
I see.

02:42.155 --> 02:45.192
It does look a bit calm.

02:46.493 --> 02:47.494
Let's hurry.

02:49.229 --> 02:51.565
The slack tide only lasts
up to three hours.

02:59.840 --> 03:00.941
Wait for me!

03:04.177 --> 03:05.212
Wait.

03:06.012 --> 03:07.280
I told you to wait for me!

03:37.777 --> 03:39.246
Will you stand up? You're heavy.

03:43.316 --> 03:44.384
You didn't have to say that...

03:47.087 --> 03:49.389
Hey, you jerks!

03:53.493 --> 03:54.394
Baek Su Jeong?

03:55.929 --> 03:56.863
Seo Anna.

03:57.130 --> 03:58.331
I was a fool...

03:59.766 --> 04:01.134
for trusting you.

04:02.669 --> 04:04.337
You bitch!

04:04.337 --> 04:06.206
Hey, you're going to fall!

04:09.676 --> 04:11.878
Stop pretending to be all nice!

04:12.679 --> 04:13.980
What are you talking about?

04:13.980 --> 04:16.149
You said you're not interested
in Deok Hyun!

04:16.149 --> 04:18.752
How could you do this to me?

04:18.752 --> 04:20.420
I told you! I'm not!

04:20.420 --> 04:22.722
You said you didn't think
he was sexy at all!

04:22.989 --> 04:24.024
Sexy?

04:24.024 --> 04:25.258
Him? "Sexy"?

04:25.258 --> 04:26.159
Hey!

04:40.841 --> 04:41.775
Deok Hyun.

04:42.042 --> 04:43.176
Me first.

04:43.677 --> 04:45.478
I got hurt more than her.

04:48.882 --> 04:50.383
Take care of it by yourselves.

04:52.185 --> 04:53.520
Where are you going?

04:53.820 --> 04:55.488
I'm hurting over here.

04:55.488 --> 04:57.490
You should patch me up!

04:57.490 --> 04:58.825
Deok Hyun!

04:59.092 --> 05:00.193
Hey!

05:00.193 --> 05:01.461
I'll do it for you. Hang on.

05:03.263 --> 05:04.264
Come here.

05:08.134 --> 05:09.536
Stay still.

05:11.505 --> 05:14.241
You think this will make me forgive you?

05:15.509 --> 05:18.078
It's not what you think.

05:18.478 --> 05:19.613
Don't lie to me.

05:20.013 --> 05:21.781
You were diving together,

05:21.781 --> 05:24.284
eating together,
working out together,

05:24.584 --> 05:26.887
and touching each other...

05:27.787 --> 05:28.655
Hey!

05:28.989 --> 05:30.824
I like men with brighter skin,

05:30.824 --> 05:32.158
and men who are sweet.

05:32.659 --> 05:33.827
That's what I mean.

05:34.394 --> 05:35.595
Deok Hyun...

05:35.595 --> 05:38.465
has a sweet face!

05:39.799 --> 05:41.168
Su Jeong.

05:44.371 --> 05:45.305
You and I...

05:45.906 --> 05:46.907
are no longer besties.

05:47.607 --> 05:49.709
This is war, you traitor.

05:50.210 --> 05:53.513
Don't ever call me by my first name again.

05:54.147 --> 05:55.982
Seo Anna!

06:01.154 --> 06:02.956
We weren't even besties
in the first place.

06:05.025 --> 06:06.493
It's been ten years since we met.

06:29.649 --> 06:30.684
Aren't we going diving?

06:31.484 --> 06:32.919
I told you earlier,

06:33.220 --> 06:35.388
the slack tide only lasts
up to three hours.

06:37.424 --> 06:38.291
Plus,

06:39.292 --> 06:41.428
you should keep that wound dry
for a while.

06:45.432 --> 06:46.366
You know,

06:47.534 --> 06:48.902
you're rude,

06:49.736 --> 06:51.071
but you're strangely nice.

06:52.005 --> 06:52.939
That's ridiculous.

06:58.411 --> 07:00.580
Even if we didn't dive,
you should wash and dry that.

07:01.014 --> 07:02.883
Any salt on it can cause corrosion.

07:04.684 --> 07:05.886
Yeah, yeah.

07:07.621 --> 07:08.889
I shouldn't have said anything.

07:09.956 --> 07:12.893
And you should make up with your friend.

07:14.794 --> 07:15.695
Why?

07:15.695 --> 07:17.464
Are you worried rumors will spread...

07:17.464 --> 07:18.999
about you two-timing us?

07:21.201 --> 07:23.436
There's a right timing in relationships,
just like the sea.

07:24.838 --> 07:26.139
Once you miss it,

07:27.807 --> 07:29.476
that timing might not return
for a long time.

07:34.915 --> 07:36.216
I guess I'm meddling.

07:44.057 --> 07:44.991
What was that?

07:46.193 --> 07:47.127
Acting like he's all cool...

07:52.065 --> 07:54.901
(Parang-ri diver Jo Mi Hyun)

07:54.901 --> 07:55.769
Well,

07:56.203 --> 07:57.504
it's true that I pushed aside
everything...

07:58.338 --> 07:59.739
apart from swimming.

08:00.874 --> 08:02.008
(EAT SLEEP SWIM)

08:02.008 --> 08:03.910
Stop sending me food.

08:04.377 --> 08:06.012
I can't even eat it all.

08:06.713 --> 08:08.615
I can take care of myself,

08:09.115 --> 08:10.917
so stop worrying.

08:12.419 --> 08:13.854
I said it's fine!

08:15.789 --> 08:17.424
"I'm busy now, so later."

08:21.361 --> 08:23.129
"I can talk to her next time."

08:23.864 --> 08:24.831
"Later."

08:44.651 --> 08:47.587
That little brat.
How could she not touch any of this?

08:50.156 --> 08:51.725
That's so hurtful.

08:54.995 --> 08:56.496
I kept telling myself "later,"

08:57.164 --> 08:58.131
and in the end...

08:59.199 --> 09:00.367
I hurt her.

09:16.116 --> 09:17.184
I missed...

09:18.585 --> 09:19.586
an important timing.

09:20.787 --> 09:23.690
(Parang-ri diver Jo Mi Hyun)

09:28.361 --> 09:29.296
How am I...

09:30.564 --> 09:32.199
supposed to make up with her?

10:12.239 --> 10:13.273
Are these red beans?

10:14.307 --> 10:15.976
Jeez. I have no idea.

10:17.043 --> 10:19.479
This isn't some supermarket.

10:20.146 --> 10:21.248
There won't be red beans.

10:21.948 --> 10:23.583
Even if there are,
it's not the right season.

10:27.354 --> 10:29.589
Red beans are planted in the summer
and harvested in the fall.

10:32.692 --> 10:33.960
Thanks for the info.

10:40.133 --> 10:40.967
What?

10:41.234 --> 10:42.202
You said there aren't any.

10:42.502 --> 10:44.137
I just said it's not harvest season yet.

10:44.137 --> 10:45.405
These are from last year.

10:47.741 --> 10:48.775
Thank you.

11:34.354 --> 11:35.255
Hey!

11:36.323 --> 11:37.157
Hey!

11:38.992 --> 11:41.728
Help me so I won't miss that timing.

11:48.335 --> 11:49.870
Come on.

11:55.208 --> 11:56.109
Open it.

12:04.584 --> 12:06.453
Stir it like this.

12:31.378 --> 12:32.179
All right.

12:33.046 --> 12:34.948
Keep stirring.

13:08.481 --> 13:09.482
If you think about it,

13:10.050 --> 13:11.384
everything's about timing.

13:19.893 --> 13:20.861
Diving,

13:21.728 --> 13:22.629
relationships,

13:23.964 --> 13:24.898
and even dough.

13:25.999 --> 13:27.334
It's all about timing.

13:57.397 --> 13:58.565
How long do I have to do this?

13:59.366 --> 14:00.600
Bring it here.

15:06.833 --> 15:07.667
Look.

15:48.808 --> 15:50.076
Like how even this honey bread...

15:50.944 --> 15:52.245
requires patience...

15:53.280 --> 15:55.015
and the right moment,

15:56.183 --> 15:58.552
everything has the right timing.

16:05.192 --> 16:06.326
Come on. Try it.

16:22.776 --> 16:24.144
Come to Parang Elementary School.

16:24.144 --> 16:26.112
Right now!

16:39.259 --> 16:42.395
That brat. Why did she make me
come all the way here?

16:49.336 --> 16:50.303
Hey!

16:57.477 --> 16:58.678
Baek Su Jeong. What is it?

16:59.079 --> 17:01.081
You called me here, but you're late.

17:02.349 --> 17:03.283
Here!

17:03.283 --> 17:04.484
Have these on the way to Seoul.

17:11.658 --> 17:12.659
Honey bread?

17:13.093 --> 17:14.528
I'm already sick of this bread,

17:14.528 --> 17:15.929
and you want me to eat it in Seoul too?

17:16.763 --> 17:19.900
You didn't even tell me
you were going to Seoul,

17:20.901 --> 17:23.003
so I didn't have time to prepare a gift.

17:32.112 --> 17:32.979
Seriously?

17:33.280 --> 17:34.981
You think some honey bread
will make us even?

17:35.815 --> 17:37.217
It's not just some honey bread.

17:37.851 --> 17:38.985
You said it yourself...

17:39.553 --> 17:42.656
that honey bread
is a way of wishing someone a safe trip.

17:49.329 --> 17:51.097
You should eat them on the way.

17:52.732 --> 17:55.702
Eating it here or on the way,
it's all the same.

17:55.702 --> 17:56.636
No, it isn't!

17:56.937 --> 17:58.205
My dad told me...

17:58.471 --> 18:01.942
honey bread lasts a long time
because of all the syrup.

18:02.309 --> 18:04.611
That's why Mom
always makes them for Dad...

18:04.611 --> 18:06.479
when he goes out to sea.

18:08.715 --> 18:10.450
It's a way of wishing him a safe trip.

18:24.998 --> 18:26.032
So...

18:26.399 --> 18:27.734
it's not just some honey bread.

18:28.835 --> 18:29.870
It's my greeting.

18:32.439 --> 18:33.406
Thanks to you,

18:34.641 --> 18:35.775
I had a safe trip.

18:36.443 --> 18:37.377
Baek Su Jeong.

18:39.346 --> 18:41.147
Don't be silly.

18:43.617 --> 18:45.719
What? Are you crying?

18:47.954 --> 18:49.055
No, I'm not!

18:49.489 --> 18:50.690
My throat's just dry from eating this.

18:55.662 --> 18:57.631
What? Did you just laugh?

18:57.831 --> 18:59.699
Yeah, I did! So what?

19:02.435 --> 19:03.436
How is it?

19:03.436 --> 19:04.437
Is it good?

19:04.638 --> 19:05.805
It's my first time making them.

19:09.042 --> 19:10.076
They're really...

19:13.246 --> 19:14.181
tasty.

19:18.051 --> 19:20.320
That doesn't mean I'm going
to let you have Deok Hyun.

19:20.520 --> 19:21.922
Don't even think about it.

19:23.723 --> 19:25.125
I told you, I'm not interested!

19:25.125 --> 19:26.193
You'd better not be lying.

19:28.395 --> 19:29.830
- What?
- It's raining.

19:29.830 --> 19:30.664
It's raining!

19:32.766 --> 19:34.668
The weather was so nice, though!

19:35.368 --> 19:36.203
Run!

19:58.124 --> 20:00.293
There's a typhoon coming.
We won't be able to dive for a while.

20:00.293 --> 20:01.127
What?

20:04.331 --> 20:05.499
What are you waiting for? Help me out.

20:09.236 --> 20:10.237
Everything...

20:10.837 --> 20:11.838
has the right timing.

20:14.641 --> 20:17.410
Typhoon Bambi is quickly moving north.

20:17.777 --> 20:21.181
Heavy rain and strong winds
are continuing nationwide,

20:21.181 --> 20:24.651
with downpours exceeding 80mm per hour
along the southern coast,

20:24.651 --> 20:27.821
raising concerns about damage.

20:28.054 --> 20:30.590
The typhoon is expected
to be at its strongest...

20:30.590 --> 20:32.025
between tonight
and early tomorrow morning.

20:33.793 --> 20:34.694
Darn it!

20:36.463 --> 20:37.464
Jeez!

20:39.399 --> 20:41.034
What are you doing? Hurry up.

20:41.034 --> 20:42.369
Just wait, all right?

20:44.371 --> 20:45.605
Hold it properly!

20:48.975 --> 20:49.809
Darn it!

21:01.354 --> 21:02.722
While waiting for the right time,

21:03.423 --> 21:05.058
hardships may come,

21:05.725 --> 21:07.060
and things may fall apart,

21:16.736 --> 21:18.238
but even the roughest typhoon...

21:19.072 --> 21:20.507
passes eventually.

21:37.324 --> 21:38.291
Shall we go today?

21:42.762 --> 21:43.697
Diving.

22:04.384 --> 22:07.420
Just as the sea gives birth to new life...

22:11.825 --> 22:14.160
after the typhoon passes
and washes away the impurities,

22:19.499 --> 22:20.400
the right timing...

22:21.601 --> 22:22.636
arrives.

22:27.574 --> 22:28.475
Let's go.

22:42.556 --> 22:43.657
Wait!

22:46.393 --> 22:47.594
Who dives...

22:50.463 --> 22:51.531
on an empty stomach?

22:53.400 --> 22:55.368
I dive on an empty stomach.

22:56.002 --> 22:58.171
Oh, dear.

22:58.638 --> 23:02.075
Then you can have this for lunch.

23:03.310 --> 23:04.144
What about me?

23:04.644 --> 23:05.745
I can eat right now.

23:06.813 --> 23:08.048
I don't have any...

23:08.915 --> 23:09.916
for you.

23:15.088 --> 23:15.956
You can do it!

23:47.687 --> 23:48.855
Let's dive here.

23:52.459 --> 23:53.827
This is different from swimming.

23:54.728 --> 23:57.030
You have to hold your breath,
not breathe out.

23:58.899 --> 24:00.167
Hold my breath...

24:02.502 --> 24:03.803
Then I'll see you down there.

25:11.271 --> 25:13.206
I can't tell anything apart.

25:19.880 --> 25:21.314
Where did you get that?

25:22.349 --> 25:24.217
You didn't buy that, did you?

25:24.651 --> 25:26.620
Did you forget everything I taught you?

25:26.620 --> 25:28.255
I remember!

25:28.522 --> 25:29.689
But it's easier said than done.

25:31.324 --> 25:32.459
Put on your goggles.

25:35.562 --> 25:36.429
And...

25:37.397 --> 25:38.331
give me your hand.

25:38.932 --> 25:39.766
What?

25:42.169 --> 25:43.837
Take a deep breath.

26:25.645 --> 26:27.914
Once you go underwater,
it'll probably look like this.

26:28.982 --> 26:30.851
That's just a rock.

26:33.353 --> 26:34.254
Do you see these?

26:37.858 --> 26:38.725
Breathing holes?

26:41.695 --> 26:43.697
Rocks don't have holes like this.

26:44.564 --> 26:46.666
When you look closely...

26:47.133 --> 26:48.735
among the rocks underwater,

26:49.369 --> 26:51.137
you'll sense the abalones breathing.

27:52.599 --> 27:53.600
I got it!

27:54.034 --> 27:55.168
I got one!

27:56.036 --> 27:56.870
What?

27:57.404 --> 27:58.505
What did you get?

27:59.172 --> 28:00.173
An abalone!

28:05.011 --> 28:06.179
An abalone!

28:06.680 --> 28:08.682
You really are Parang-ri's mermaid.

28:08.682 --> 28:11.051
Seo Anna, nice!

28:15.088 --> 28:16.056
Look!

28:23.096 --> 28:25.532
Don't get ahead of yourself
just because you got one.

28:25.532 --> 28:26.967
Dive only as long
as you can hold your breath.

28:27.400 --> 28:28.568
Quit nagging.

28:30.403 --> 28:33.406
I've been waiting for this day, you know.

28:33.840 --> 28:34.808
So trust me.

28:35.842 --> 28:36.843
I'll see you underwater.

30:18.612 --> 30:20.347
If I keep waiting for the right moment,

30:21.615 --> 30:22.716
will my dream...

30:24.351 --> 30:25.886
ever shine...

30:27.587 --> 30:28.522
again?

30:46.506 --> 30:47.774
Are you that happy?

30:48.608 --> 30:49.609
Yes.

30:49.609 --> 30:50.510
Thanks to you.

30:53.113 --> 30:54.014
And since I'm in a good mood,

30:55.549 --> 30:57.751
I'll take back what I said about you.

31:00.487 --> 31:01.888
About you being rude...

31:02.756 --> 31:04.457
but strangely nice.

31:04.991 --> 31:05.926
Yes?

31:07.027 --> 31:10.197
You're not rude,
but you're not nice either.

31:12.465 --> 31:14.334
Isn't that worse, then?

31:15.001 --> 31:16.069
But...

31:16.870 --> 31:19.005
you're like the sea.

31:23.243 --> 31:25.679
On the surface, you push others away
like rough waves,

31:26.513 --> 31:28.181
but you're actually deep and quiet inside.

31:30.083 --> 31:31.017
So...

31:31.985 --> 31:33.320
though I haven't known you long,

31:34.721 --> 31:36.189
I feel like I can trust you.

31:43.296 --> 31:44.865
You're a bad judge of character.

31:46.399 --> 31:47.634
I know you feel good.

31:48.535 --> 31:49.469
In any case,

31:50.203 --> 31:51.238
thank you.

31:55.842 --> 31:56.877
For teaching me...

31:57.644 --> 31:58.712
diving.

32:38.485 --> 32:39.286
Hey.

32:39.819 --> 32:40.654
Hey.

32:44.024 --> 32:46.760
I heard this guy lives here. Is it true?

32:48.361 --> 32:49.296
Who?

32:51.965 --> 32:53.466
Oh, him!

32:53.466 --> 32:54.501
Yun Deok Hyun!

32:55.168 --> 32:56.670
That's Yun Deok Hyun!

32:57.370 --> 32:58.338
He lives over there...

32:59.039 --> 33:00.307
in the house with the red roof.

33:03.210 --> 33:05.712
But why...

33:06.713 --> 33:08.148
are you looking for Yun Deok Hyun?

33:12.786 --> 33:13.787
I'm just asking...

33:14.654 --> 33:15.488
Why?

33:18.124 --> 33:19.759
Is he someone I shouldn't be looking for?

33:21.428 --> 33:22.429
No...

33:23.163 --> 33:24.364
It's not that.

33:29.603 --> 33:32.305
I just have a debt to repay him.

33:32.305 --> 33:33.340
No need to be so scared.

33:37.811 --> 33:38.812
Wow!

33:39.346 --> 33:40.547
Living the good life, I see...

33:42.415 --> 33:43.450
Yun Deok Hyun.

34:18.919 --> 34:20.921
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
